# Step 27: the TypeScript client of the RPC protocol. The rules of where its
# test runs (`crates/cortex-cli/tests/system/ts_client.rs`), broken one at a
# time: the blocking jobs never depend on Node, a job that asks for the test
# cannot pass without running it, and a Node that cannot run the client as it
# is is never used. What the client checks of the server is broken in
# step-27.breaks, whose tests need no Node.

[break] the-blocking-jobs-run-the-typescript-client
rule: In CI the test runs only where `CORTEX_TS_CLIENT` asks for it, and looks for no Node otherwise, so the blocking jobs never depend on Node.
file: crates/cortex-cli/tests/system/ts_client.rs
in: here
find: if ci && !asked {
replace: if ci && !asked && false {
caught-by:
    cortex-cli::system ts_client::it_runs_where_it_is_asked_for_and_never_in_ci_unasked

[break] a-job-that-asks-for-the-client-passes-without-node
rule: Where `CORTEX_TS_CLIENT` is set, a missing or older Node fails the test rather than leaving it not run.
file: crates/cortex-cli/tests/system/ts_client.rs
in: here
find: Err(problem) if asked => Here::Wanting(problem)
replace: Err(problem) if asked => Here::NotRun(problem)
caught-by:
    cortex-cli::system ts_client::it_runs_where_it_is_asked_for_and_never_in_ci_unasked

[break] a-node-older-than-22-18-is-used
rule: A Node of the 22 line older than 22.18 is not used: it does not strip a file's types by itself, so it cannot run the client as it is.
file: crates/cortex-cli/tests/system/ts_client.rs
in: strips_types
find: 22 => minor >= 18
replace: 22 => minor >= 6
caught-by:
    cortex-cli::system ts_client::it_runs_where_it_is_asked_for_and_never_in_ci_unasked
